1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,943
To write a new part,
start with a new track.

2
00:00:05,143 --> 00:00:11,300
Name it after its instrument: the name
is how MIDI-GPT knows what to write.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,443
The full list of names
is in INSTRUMENTS.md.

4
00:00:15,643 --> 00:00:21,014
Create an empty MIDI item over
the bars you want, and select it.

5
00:00:21,214 --> 00:00:26,871
MIDI-GPT only writes into MIDI items,
so the empty item is required.

6
00:00:27,071 --> 00:00:32,514
Tick "A" (autoregressive): it
writes the whole track, bar by bar.

7
00:00:32,714 --> 00:00:39,229
On an empty track, set the controls
yourself. Here: one or two voices at a time.

8
00:00:41,429 --> 00:00:45,443
Select the context bars
and click "Generate".

9
00:00:50,643 --> 00:00:54,014
A new cello part that fits the song.
